  "evidence": "TEXT_D: Freeze non‑essential immigration; detain and deport illegal entrants; bar asylum from safe countries; leave the ECHR if needed; create a Department of Immigration. Zero‑tolerance policing, more stop and search, mandatory life for repeat violent offenders, 10,000 new prison places. \"Patriotic\" curriculum; ban transgender ideology in schools; single‑sex spaces; replace the Equalities Act; British Bill of Rights; reject WHO treaty/WEF/CBDC. Assert UK sovereignty: scrap retained EU law, abandon Windsor Framework, prepare TCA renegotiation. Prioritise national identity and protectionism: buy British; restrict foreign access to UK waters; protect country sports.\n\nTEXT_E: Uphold the ECHR; Race Equality Act; disability/ethnicity pay‑gap reporting; full ban on conversion practices; modernised gender recognition law; votes at 16. Clean‑energy push (zero‑carbon electricity by 2030; restore 2030 ICE phase‑out; no new oil and gas licences). Law‑and‑order measures (Neighbourhood Policing Guarantee; bans on machetes/zombie knives; tougher shoplifting rules) and a New Border Security Command with a pledge to reduce net migration via tougher enforcement.",
  "reasoning": "The electorate profile leans TAN (0.60), and TEXT_D argues consistently from TAN commitments—national sovereignty over supranational authority, restrictive immigration, strong law‑and‑order, and defense of traditional social norms—whereas TEXT_E mixes some TAN elements with pronounced GAL commitments on equality, LGBT rights, and an ambitious green transition. Therefore, TEXT_D sits closer to the TAN‑leaning profile than TEXT_E, which trends more GAL overall.",
